# TEST_MODE : MULTI_MODULE_OK

# Lambdas in the body of a generic declared in a HEADER, instantiated by two
# separately compiled modules.
#
# A lambda's name hashes env.inf.name, and a generic body is replayed in the
# generic's own file -- the header -- so both modules named their lambda the
# same, and it was a public symbol:
#
#     multiple definition of `L51B1FEBCEBAAF5CD_LT_0003'
#
# Lambda procedures are module-private now, like a generic instantiation's
# procedures.  The modules are the same shape on purpose, so the counters
# match.

MAIN := lambda-generic-mm-main.bas
SRCS := lambda-generic-mm-a.bas lambda-generic-mm-b.bas
